{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"prompt\": \"Use case: stylized-concept. Create a landscape 3:2 Minecraft builder reference sheet, crisp authentic vanilla Minecraft voxels only, skilled human builder quality, plain warm light background, no characters or animals. Title: POLARTON / HILLSIDE KIT — ROUND 1. Two main views side by side: LEFT straight-on orthographic north front elevation showing ALL EIGHT modules in one continuous sample row, numbered 0–7 in order, no missing buildings; RIGHT three-quarter southeast view looking uphill showing ALL EIGHT buildings installed on the actual site in reference image 2. Reference image 1 is the architectural mood board: develop its stronger sample-row take, with sturdy varied massing and actual block-sized construction. Reference image 2 is the binding terrain reference: preserve its stream at the east/right, existing village foreground, westward climb, plateau, terraced pads, spruce plot fences, retaining walls, driveways and winding streets, never flatten or invent a different hill. Keep right-view buildings readable, avoid hiding any behind another. Same block scale in both views; row may use more horizontal space. Minimal neat labels, small bottom palette and two compact technical inset diagrams if space permits; architecture takes priority.\\nROW GEOMETRY: exactly 96 blocks wide. Lane x=0..95,z=0..4, dirt and gravel. Eight plots, each 12 wide x 14 deep, z=5..18; plot i x=12i..12i+11. Every roof, eave, chimney and porch inside plot. North is toward viewer/lane. Identical spruce_fence perimeter, two spruce_fence_gate blocks centered at local x=5,6, lantern posts at both front corners. Front yard z=5..8. Ground floor at most one above yard; each main entrance a two-wide bottom slab ramp, half-block rises only, maximum three half steps before landing at least 2x2, final cell before door level. No entry stairs. Real roof verges, eaves and ridges, recessed framed windows, projecting porch beams, trapdoor detailing.\\nMODULES in left row order:\\n0 COTTON GIN: two-storey stripped spruce timber and pale birch board house on stone piers, dark deepslate slate gable roof, wide front wagon bay, upper hay door with projecting hoist beam. Clear machinery bay reserved for owner's Create gin, no mod machine blocks; mark a shaft opening in floor and wall.\\n1 SCHOOL: small white one-room clapboard school, deepslate roof, little bell cupola, cloakroom porch, yard bench, cartography_table inside.\\n2 FARMHOUSE: 1.5 storeys weathered spruce and birch boards, warm spruce shingle roof, deep front porch, rear kitchen ell, composter. Four beds upstairs, table and stove by wall hearth.\\n3 BLACKSMITH/WHEELWRIGHT: open-front timber forge shed, deepslate roof, own straight masonry chimney set into side wall, anvil and smithing_table, wheel in progress represented with vanilla trapdoors and grindstone, block-built cart beneath lean-to.\\n4 CHURCH: white_concrete clapboard-like walls with calcite trim, tall narrow steeple visible from below, deepslate roof, lectern by entrance, small side graveyard with low white birch_fence pickets entirely INSIDE outer spruce boundary.\\n5 TOBACCO BARN: tall narrow spruce vertical board structure, spruce shingle roof, vent gaps, stacked hanging drying tiers of brown/green vanilla vegetation inside, base fire hearth/flue.\\n6 CORN CRIB + GRANARY: pale birch slatted crib on stone piers, adjacent little granary and accessible slab ramp, hay_block corn storage, sacks suggested by mushroom_stem blocks, scale made from chain and iron_trapdoor.\\n7 OWNER HOUSE: two-storey bricks and birch trim, oxidized copper roof, wraparound porch, projecting bay and balcony toward village; four beds, table, stove by wall hearth. Refined but compact, fully within 12x14.\\nSITE PLACEMENT in right view: row0 gin goes site1 lowland near village facing north; row1 school site2 plateau faces west; row2 farmhouse site3 plateau faces east; row3 forge si